{"format":1,"seq":194,"writes":[{"type":"entry","value":{"model":[{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm checking NVDA's P/E and market cap figures against plausible late-2026 levels, flagging TSLA as an outlier, and the market-cap-weighted P/E of the other seven mega-caps comes out near 25x — worth comparing against the 2000 dot-com leaders like Cisco, Microsoft, Intel, and Oracle.\n\nFrom memory Cisco traded around 200x trailing earnings and Microsoft near 70x at the end of 1999, which I'll cite with appropriate hedging since I'm not fully certain of exact figures.\n\nThe strongest echo of 1999 seems to be the rate shock: the Fed cut through early 2026 then started hiking again, and the 10-year yield jumped roughly 100bp over ten months and 45bp in just the last two — similar to the bond shock that preceded the 2000 top.\n\nNow I need to check the pre-commit hook setup so the commit doesn't fail, then move on to building the charts and writing the report — pulling the Yahoo data again, generating four charts, assembling the markdown, and saving a CSV alongside it.\n\nI'm placing the report at `docs/research/2026-11-dotcom-analog.md` with a companion CSV containing month, S&P, Nasdaq, and CAPE columns, while making sure formatting tools won't choke on the markdown file.\n\nFor the charts: the first rebases S&P 500 and Nasdaq to 100 starting from the Netscape IPO versus the ChatGPT launch, using month-index labels across both 48-month windows. The second chart projects forward from today under the assumption that the 1999-analog pattern continues, plotting hypothetical S&P trajectories against actual calendar months out to around 2030.\n\nI also want a CAPE ratio chart from 1990–2026 with constant reference lines for the 1999 peak (44.2) and the long-run median around 16, plus a rolling 5-year and 3-year annualized return chart for the S&P over the same period. I'm also considering a fifth chart comparing Fed funds rate and 10-year yield trajectories across both eras using the same month-aligned structure.\n\nThe rate comparison is striking: in the 1999 analog, the rate hikes happened around months 41-48 (Jan-Aug 1999, 4.72% to 5.94%), and today's cycle shows almost the same pattern at months 37-47 (Dec 2025 to Oct 2026, 4.14% to 5.13%) — definitely including this chart, trimming to 0-47 months since FRED data stops at October 2026.\n\nI'm also calculating current drawdowns from recent highs: the S&P is down about 1.2% from its September 2026 peak of 7651.54, while the Nasdaq is down roughly 6.8% from its May 2026 high of 26972.\n\nLet me check the husky hook setup and consolidate everything into a single program, injecting the chart.xy function appropriately.\n\n","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_bdrk_01HErxzcRA74Abu2Fgic8VBh","name":"typescript","arguments":{"code":"// @pit: {\"label\": \"Read husky pre-commit hook and oxfmt config before writing report\"}\nasync ({ workspace: { read } }) => {\n  const [h, f, c] = await Promise.all([read(\".husky/pre-commit\", { format: \"raw\" }), read(\".oxfmtrc.json\", { format: \"raw\" }), read(\"docs/charts.md\", { format: \"raw\", limit: 30 })]);\n  return { hook: h.content, fmt: f.content, charts: c.content } as PitJsonValue;\n}"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"nvidia","model":"aws/anthropic/bedrock-claude-opus-5-5","usage":{"input":2,"output":1997,"cacheRead":59971,"cacheWrite":5944,"totalTokens":67914,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0,"totalFromProvider":false},"cacheWrite1h":0,"reasoning":1776},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1794856500969,"responseId":"msg_bdrk_3v5mg4k6h3o26u7kex6txyjwjsitcy5lhegtt22ozex3z752thba","rawStopReason":"tool_use","durationMs":24686,"thinkingLevel":"high"}],"kind":"pi.assistant","id":57,"conversationId":1,"byTaskId":56}},{"type":"task","value":{"id":56,"conversationId":1,"kind":"pi.generation","version":2,"input":{},"background":false,"abortRequested":false,"s